      "title_text": "'Direct Expenses' amounts on vouchers with a cash or bank line on their side are not attributed to the party (or parties) on the other side",
      "limits_sha256_16": "5bd195122ffc31b2",
      "limits_text": [
        "On each voucher cited (none of them a sales, purchase, credit or debit note voucher) a party ledger, or more than one, is on the other side from the 'Direct Expenses' lines, and a cash or bank line is on the same side as them. These lines may be a deduction from what was paid or received, for example bank charges deducted from a customer's receipt, or a discount allowed on it, or something else on the same voucher; the books do not say which, so they are shown in the row 'Not attributed to a party', not under any party, and are in the block's Total row. A round-off on a receipt is listed here too. This applies to the expense blocks only."
